    "buggy_baseline_is_parent": true,
    "single_parent_matches_baseline": true,
    "commit_message": "Fix off-by-one error when decoding root-level null, true, and false\n\nThe guards for checking if there are enough bytes to parse literal values\nused `>` instead of `>=`, causing failures when the input is exactly the\nliteral with no trailing characters.\n\nFor example, decoding `null` (4 bytes) would fail because `count > 4` is\nfalse when count equals 4.\n\nChanges:\n- `null`: `count > 4` → `count >= 4`\n- `true`: `count > 4` → `count >= 4`\n- `false`: `count > 5` → `count >= 5`\n\nAdded test case `testRootLevelPrimitiveDecoding` to prevent regression.",
    "boundary_evidence": "repair/boundary-verification.json",
    "boundary_evidence_sha256": "6b1ae010b8b88d35fb78de8fe3ddf6bedc35bce8159f3562816e875837583d96"
